{"base_rate":0.13324538258575197,"brier":0.07356306068601583,"bss":0.36304102958241025,"bss_hi":0.47276181310949583,"bss_lo":0.2318334199329437,"country":"MX","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.03137203166226915,"ess":311.6352270912071,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Reynosa</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Reynosa rain forecast is genuinely useful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (76%), believe about\n<b>66%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 758 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMCALLEN MILLER INTL AP, 11.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.36, ranked 43 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(18&ndash;83) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>280</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>90</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>76%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Reynosa</b> <span class=\"muted\">MX</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.36</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>18&ndash;83\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>758 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Reynosa &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Reynosa\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 61.54,367.63157894736844 68.148,357.73333333333335 82.37153846153846,335.3333333333333 110.91368421052633,295.7894736842105 171.4548148148148,229.20987654320987 325.5228571428572,79.45454545454544 325.5228571428572,140.9090909090909 171.4548148148148,301.1111111111111 110.91368421052633,353.2631578947368 82.37153846153846,377.3333333333333 68.148,382.0 61.54,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"333.4986807387863\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"333.4986807387863\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,380.7 61.54,372.42105263157896 68.148,377.9555555555556 82.37153846153846,358.6666666666667 110.91368421052633,348.4736842105263 171.4548148148148,229.20987654320987 325.5228571428572,140.9090909090909\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 280 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"380.7\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"61.54\" cy=\"372.42105263157896\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 90 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.148\" cy=\"377.9555555555556\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"82.37153846153846\" cy=\"358.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"110.91368421052633\" cy=\"348.4736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"171.4548148148148\" cy=\"229.20987654320987\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 76%&amp;#10;It rained 66% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"325.5228571428572\" cy=\"140.9090909090909\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(13%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Reynosa the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.44) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.04).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'>-0.043</td><td class='num'>9.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'>0.325</td><td class='num'>5.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>0.432</td><td class='num'>4.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'>0.442</td><td class='num'>3.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":26.08005,"lon":-98.28456,"n":758,"n_cities":109,"name":"Reynosa","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":280,"obs":0.0035714285714285713,"sig":true},{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.01,"n":76,"obs":0.02631578947368421,"sig":false},{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.028666666666666667,"n":90,"obs":0.011111111111111112,"sig":false},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.06884615384615385,"n":78,"obs":0.06